    {
      "case": "1840 and 2056 printed Sydney Mail witnesses, Covington gaps and monetary/prospective distinctions",
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-1840",
        "DCP-LETT-2056"
      ],
      "requirement": "Preserve both Darwin-to-Covington texts as printed witnesses: 1840 is sourced from Sydney Mail 9 August 1884 with a later de Beer 1959 variant, and its manuscript is missing; 2056 likewise has Sydney Mail 1884 and de Beer 1959 sources listed in TEI, not a recovered manuscript. The September 4 and September 14 Covington letters are acknowledged with approximate arrival wording, but their texts remain missing. Keep Darwin’s heard Beagle-collier report attributed and retain the later editorial correction in apparatus, not as body voice. Render the 40 sovereigns as the Royal Society medal’s weight comparison, not a payment of forty coins or a salary; the medal itself was received. Keep FitzRoy lunch and William’s barrister plan prospective.",
